 China\nEast Asia and Australasia\nEurope\nLatin America & Caribbean\nNorth America\nSouth East Asia\nUK\nApplication Guidance\nShow submenu for Application Guidance\nInternational Country-Specific Qualifications\nEnglish Language Requirements\nSupport Services\nHow To Apply\nUK Qualifications\nFees and Funding\nShow submenu for Fees and Funding\nFee Status and Payment\nForeign Loans\nInternational Scholarships, Awards and Bursaries\nLiving Costs\nApplication Fees and Post Offer Deposits (PG)\nCollege Residence Charges\nVisas\nShow submenu for Visas\nConfirmation of Acceptance for Studies (CAS)\nApplying for a Student Visa\nStudent Visa Requirements\nYour Family\nStudent Visa: Money Required\nStudying as a Visitor\nArrivals\nShow submenu for Arrivals\nInternational Meet and Greet service\nInformation for pre-sessional students\nWhat to bring\nLife in Durham and the UK\nThings to do in Durham\nMeet and Greet FAQs\nPathway Programmes\nShow submenu for Pathway Programmes\nInternational Foundation Year\nPre-Masters\nEnglish Preparation\nInternational Entry Requirements\nWe accept a wide range of qualifications from the UK and the rest of the world for entry to our undergraduate courses. Entry requirements per course will differ, and some courses may require previous study in certain subjects. You can find the entry requirements for your chosen degree on UCAS Course Search or the Durham Courses Database.\nWe understand that some students may have a combination of qualifications, and if you have any questions about how we assess those qualifications together you can use our Contact Form.\nDetails included under each country are for future undergraduate and postgraduate taught students. If you are interested in a postgraduate research course, please visit Postgraduate Study and our Academic Departments.\nEnglish Language Requirements\nYou may be required to submit an English Language qualification if you are not a native English speaker. Please review the standard English Language Requirements for your course and country.\nPathway programmes at the Durham University International Study Centre\nInternational students who do not meet the requirements for direct entry to an undergraduate or postgraduate degree, you may be eligible to take a pathway programme at the Durham University International Study Centre. Located at our Queen\u2019s Campus, the International Study Centre provides a supportive environment where you will be introduced to the style of teaching you will experience should you progress on to your degree. Programmes aim to improve your academic knowledge, study and English language skills. Completing your pathway programme at the International Study Centre and achieving the required grades means that you can progress to your degree at Durham University City Campus.\nYou can choose from English Preparation, International Foundation Year or Pre-Masters pathway programmes.\nFind Out More\nInternational Country-Specific Qualifications\nIf you aren\u2019t studying in a majority English-speaking country, then you will need to demonstrate English language proficiency through an accepted English language test.\nEuropean Country-Specific Qualifications\nAll courses require you to achieve certain grades in your qualifications, and some require prior study and knowledge of specific subjects, which we\u2019ll ask you to achieve at a particular grade.\nInternational Country-Specific Qualifications\nIf you aren\u2019t studying in a majority English-speaking country, then you will need to demonstrate English language proficiency through an accepted English language test.\nEuropean Country-Specific Qualifications\nAll courses require you to achieve certain grades in your qualifications, and some require prior study and knowledge of specific subjects, which we\u2019ll ask you to achieve at a particular grade.\nYour Durham prospectus\nOrder your personalised prospectus and College guide here.\nOrder Now\nQuestions about studying here?\nCheck out our list of FAQs or submit an enquiry form.\nAsk us\nInternational Study Centre\nTake the first step to a degree from a world-leading university, and one of the oldest in the UK. Our international programmes have been created with your needs in mind. Start your pathway to university.\nFind Out More\nContact Durham University\nAbout us\nDurham University on Bluesky\nDurham University on Twitter\nDurham University on Facebook\nDurham University on LinkedIn\nDurham University on YouTube\nDurham University on Instagram\nDurham University on TikTok\nThe University\nAbout us\nJobs\nContact us\nVisit us\nOur Colleges\nAcademic Departments\nCeremonies\nStatements and policies\nNotices\nStatement on Modern Slavery\nFreedom of expression\nWebsite accessibility\nStudent complaints and non-academic misconduct\nSafeguarding\nBusiness services\nHelping business\nAnalytical services\nGlobal Durham\nInternational Consortia\nResearch and partnerships\nUseful links\nLearn Ultra\nBanner Self-Service\nStaff directory\nTechnician Commitment\nDU Hub (Internal)\nIT help and support\nThe Palatine Centre\nDurham University\nStockton Road\nDurham\nDH1 3LE\nCharitable status\nDisclaimer\nTrading name\nCookie notice\nPrivacy notices\n\u00a92026 Durham University", "links": [["Skip to main content", "https://www.durham.ac.uk/study/international/entry-requirements/#main-content"], ["", "https://www.durham.ac.uk/"], ["", "https://www.durham.ac.uk/"], ["Alumni", "https://www.durham.ac.uk/alumni/"], ["Library and Collections", "https://www.durham.ac.uk/departments/library/"], ["Business School", "https://www.durham.ac.uk/business/"], ["Things To Do", "https://www.durham.ac.uk/things-to-do/"], ["About us", "https://www.durham.ac.uk/about-us/"], ["How to contact us", "https://www.durham.ac.uk/about-us/how-to-contact-us/"], ["Study", "https://www.durham.ac.uk/study/"], ["Undergraduate", "https://www.durham.ac.uk/study/undergraduate/"], ["Postgraduate", "https://www.durham.ac.uk/study/postgradua